   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to authorize the county of Clinton to reinstate and employ Aaron Heroux as a deputy sheriff",
    "basePrintNo": "S7564",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7564-2015",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Civil Service",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S7564\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to authorize the county of Clinton to reinstate and employ\nAaron Heroux as a deputy sheriff\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nAuthorizes the county of Clinton to reinstate Aaron Heroux as a deputy\nsheriff, notwithstanding that such reinstatement will occur more than\n1 year after leaving such position.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1. Authorizes the county of Clinton to reinstate Aaron Heroux\nas a deputy sheriff with the sheriff's department of such county,\nnotwithstanding the provisions of paragraph (b) of subdivision 4 of\nsection 58 of the civil service law or any other provision of the law\nto the contrary, provided he provide a written request to that effect\nwith the sheriff of the county of Clinton within one year of the\neffective date of this act.\n\nSection 2. Establishes the effective date.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nAaron Heroux was a Clinton County Deputy Sheriff from March 2002 until\nFebruary 2013, at which time he was forced to apply for disability\nretirement due to health problems related to Cystic Fibrosis. In\nFebruary of 2014, Aaron received a bilateral lung transplant at\nMassachusetts General Hospital, and has since worked to beat all\nmedical expectations and is now in full health and physical condition.\nAaron's doctors from Massachusetts General Hospital have certified\nthat he is capable of returning to work, and the Clinton County\nSheriff has recommended him for the position. Aaron has been prevented\nfrom returning to work due to Section 58 of the New York State Civil\nService Law, paragraph (a) age limit of 35 years. This bill would\nallow this dedicated civil servant to return to his position as Deputy\nSheriff, provided he files a written request with the sheriff's\ndepartment in Clinton county, and complies with the provisions of\nparagraph (c) of subdivision 1 of section 58 of the civil service law,\nwhich includes the height, weight and physical fitness requirements\nprescribed by the municipal police training council.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNone.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
